        <div class="terms-text-wrapper [max-width:1280px] max-lg:[max-width:728px] max-lg:[padding-left:20px] max-lg:[padding-right:20px]">
          <div class="rich-text w-richtext [font-family:Switzer,_sans-serif] [font-size:16px]">
            <h3>1. Introduction</h3>
            <p>Welcome to www.motiontheagency.com (“Site” or “Website”).</p>
            <p>‍</p>
            <p>Motion The Agency is the trading name of Motion The Agency LTD having registered office at 42-44 Bishopsgate, London EC2N 4AH and with trading number of 13913553.</p>
            <p>‍</p>
            <p>Motion The Agency owns and operates this website. The terms “we,” “us,” “Motion The Agency,” and “our” refer to Motion The Agency Ltd. throughout the Site. We provide you, the user, with this website, including all information, tools, and services available through this site, on the condition that you accept all of the terms, conditions, policies, and notices indicated here.</p>
            <p>‍</p>
            <p>By accessing our site, you (“User” or “Client”) agree to be governed by the following terms and conditions/terms of use (“Terms”), and any terms and policies linked herein and/or accessible by hyperlink. These Terms and Conditions apply to all site users, including browsers, clients, and/or content contributors, without limitation.</p>
            <p>‍</p>
            <p><strong>PLEASE READ THESE TERMS CAREFULLY BEFORE FURTHER USING OUR WEBSITE OR ORDERING SERVICES. IF YOU DO NOT AGREE TO ALL OF THE TERMS AND CONDITIONS THEN YOU MAY NOT ACCESS THE WEBSITE OR PURCHASE OUR SERVICES. THE SERVICES ARE ONLY MADE AVAILABLE TO BUSINESSES AND NOT TO INDIVIDUALS. </strong></p>
            <p>‍</p>
            <h3>2. General Information</h3>
            <ul role="list">
              <li><strong>About. </strong>Motion The Agency provides remote video editing, motion graphics, and design services to business clients. To find out more information about what we do, please refer to our website.</li>
              <li><strong>Sole discretion. </strong>We reserve the right to add/discontinue any product or service anytime at our sole discretion.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>‍</p>
            <h3>3. Eligibility</h3>
            <p>Our services are strictly limited to parties who are businesses and not individuals.</p>
            <p>‍</p>
            <h3><strong>4. Permitted Use </strong></h3>
            <p>You agree to use the Site and the Services only for purposes that are permitted by these Terms and in compliance with all applicable laws, regulations, and generally accepted practices or guidelines in the relevant jurisdictions. You may only use the Site and Services for your non-commercial, non-exclusive, non-assignable, non-transferable, and limited personal use, and no other purposes. You will not (and will not attempt to):</p>
            <p>‍</p>
            <ol role="list">
              <li>Access any of the Services by any means other than through the interface that is provided by Motion The Agency;</li>
              <li>Gain unauthorised access to Motion The Agency’s computer system or engage in any activity that interferes with the performance of, or impairs the functionality or security of the Site, the Services, Motion The Agency’s networks, and computer systems;</li>
              <li>Access any of the Site or the Services through any automated means or with any automated features or devices (including use of scripts or web crawlers);</li>
              <li>Access or collect any personally identifiable information, including any names, email addresses, or other such information for any purpose, including, without limitation, commercial purposes;</li>
              <li>Reproduce, duplicate, copy, sell, trade, or resell any Motion The Agency of the Site or the Services for any purpose; and</li>
              <li>Reproduce, duplicate, copy, sell, trade, or resell any products or services bearing any trademark, service mark, trade name, logo, or service mark owned by Motion The Agency in a way that is likely or intended to confuse the owner or authorised user of such marks, names or logos.</li>
            </ol>
            <p>‍</p>
            <h3><strong>5. Ownership of Materials </strong></h3>
            <p>The Client shall be the sole owner of the copyrights of the delivered project subject to full payment and successful completion of the project according to Motion The Agency. If the project is incomplete, or if the Client requests a refund or cancellation, the Client does not become the owner or retains any copyrights of the Project.</p>
            <p>‍</p>
            <p>Client warrants that any materials provided to Motion The Agency as examples of the material to be incorporated into a project during the design process are its own and do not infringe on or misappropriate any third party’s rights, including but not limited to all intellectual property rights and any right of publicity.</p>
            <p>‍</p>
            <h3><strong>6. Risk</strong></h3>
            <p>This Site is used at your own risk. You acknowledge that your use of this Site, as well as any of your communication and activity on it, is solely your responsibility. We may refuse you access to this Site on a temporary or permanent basis if we believe, in our sole discretion, that you participated in prohibited activity, were not respectful of other users, or otherwise violated the Terms and Conditions.</p>
            <p>‍</p>
            <h3><strong>7. Accounts, Registrations, and Passwords</strong></h3>
            <p>If you use this Site and it requires you to create an account and/or password(s), you are entirely responsible for keeping your account and password(s) secure and restricting access to your computer. You agree to supply us with current, complete, and accurate information as required by any forms if you establish an account, register, or otherwise give us information. Motion The Agency is not liable for any errors or delays in responding to any question or request as a result of obsolete or erroneous information given by you, or any technological issues beyond its control. </p>
            <p>‍</p>
            <h3><strong>8. Intellectual Property Rights</strong></h3>
            <p>Unless otherwise stated, the Website is the property of Motion The Agency, and all source code, databases, functionality, software, website designs, audio, video, text, photographs, and graphics of any kind and in any format (herein, collectively or individually, the “Content”), as well as the trademarks, service marks, and logos contained therein (the “Marks”), are owned and controlled by Motion The Agency. The Content and Marks are given “as is” for your personal information and use only. Without Motion The Agency’s express prior written permission, no part of the Website or Content may be copied, reproduced, aggregated, republished, uploaded, posted, displayed, encoded, translated, transmitted, distributed, sold, licensed, or otherwise exploited for any commercial purpose whatsoever.</p>
            <p>‍</p>
            <h3><strong>9. Monitoring Activity</strong></h3>
            <p>Motion The Agency has no obligation to monitor this Site or any portion thereof. However, we reserve the right to review any posted content and remove, delete, redact or otherwise modify such content, at our sole discretion, at any time and from time to time, without notice or further obligation to you. Motion The Agency has no obligation to display or post any content.  </p>
            <p>‍</p>
            <h3><strong>10. Refunds and Cancellations</strong></h3>
            <ul role="list">
              <li>All payments are to be made upfront 100% in advance by the Client to Motion The Agency in accordance with the payment method provided by Motion The Agency.</li>
              <li>You acknowledge that we will provide full refunds for content that has been created within 14 days and on the assumption that no revisions have been requested to the content provided.</li>
              <li>In the event you purchase our video editing services and change your mind to cancel it, you have the right to do so before we commence your project and a full refund will be provided.</li>
              <li>In the event we produce content and you are unsatisfied with the quality, under such circumstances, you can request a 100% refund if 0 revisions have been requested to the video.</li>
              <li>In the event of a partial refund, the content/project delivered is unusable and the Client must sign and affirm that he/she will not re-publish, sell, transfer or use the content/project in any way for any commercial purposes (see section 11 ‘Revisions’ for more information).</li>
              <li>All refunds shall be transacted in the manner or with the currency or payment type used by Client to make such payment. Upon receipt of the refund by Client, any contractual or transactional relationship between the parties shall be of no further force or effect and shall be considered void and terminated.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>‍</p>
            <h3><strong>11. Revisions</strong></h3>
            <ul role="list">
              <li>We offer revisions to our Clients and the number of revisions will be stipulated in the Client contract. Clients acknowledge and understand that Motion The Agency reserves the right to cancel any service or terminate any project.</li>
              <li>In the event the client utilises the ‘Motion The Agency Fixed Price Agreement’ this will includes, zero, five or unlimited planning revisions as stipulated on our website pricing page (<a href="https://www.motiontheagency.com/pricing/motion-graphics-price">https://www.motiontheagency.com/pricing/motion-graphics-price</a>) and 2 sets of animation revisions as standard. </li>
            </ul>
            <ul role="list">
